# Response headers, for hosts that read this file (Netlify, Cloudflare Pages).
# Vercel, where Luna is hosted, takes the same headers from vercel.json instead;
# keep the two in step. GitHub Pages ignores both and cannot send headers at all,
# which is why the content security policy is also embedded in the page as a
# <meta> tag.
#
# frame-ancestors and X-Frame-Options stop other sites framing Luna (clickjacking);
# both only work as real headers. Geolocation stays available to this site alone,
# for "Use my location"; nothing else is wanted.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(self), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
